<title>UK: Rolls-Royce sells unit to Magellan.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce sells unit to Magellan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group Rolls-Royce Plc said on Thursday it had sold Bristol Aerospace Ltd to Canadian firm Magellan Aerospace Corp for an undisclosed amount.  </p>
<p>Rolls-Royce announced in October 1996 that it was looking to sell Bristol because &quot;its capabilities were not in line with the core markets Rolls-Royce would be exploiting in the coming century&quot;.</p>
<p>Canada-based Bristol has net assets representing  around two percent of those of Rolls-Royce Plc and it employs more than 900 people.</p>
<p>Rolls-Royce said that proceeds from the sale will be used for general working capital.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
